Demon's what images are conjured into  your mind when you hear that word in  ancient Greece demons were thought of in  two ways the word demon could be used to  refer to an inner attendant or an  inspiring force in fact the famous  philosopher Socrates said that he lived  his life in accordance with the internal  dictates of his own quote demon  [Music]  in Socrates's view demons were more akin  to what we would refer to as the soul  the other view of demons in ancient  times was that they were being somewhere  in between humans and gods these demons  were not necessarily considered to be  malevolent in the ancient Greek view  demons were thought to be benign similar  in nature to the gods and humans so  widely varied they were nature spirits  forces of nature spirit guides the  rising prominence of Christianity would  change the way demons were thought of  considerably the modern view paints  demons as personifications of wickedness  and malevolence demons today are  typically thought of to be sources of or  agents of evil demons can also be viewed  metaphorically in the modern sense and  the metaphoric sense there is usually  still a negative connotation for example  a person might refer to their own mental  anguish relating to past trauma as inner  demons in this video we will discuss  various literal and metaphorical demons  in a Song of Ice and Fire using both the  archaic and modern definitions  [Music]  considering the ancient definition of  the word both the children of the forest  and the others could potentially be  considered demons the children of the  forest which Martin based on the she of  Irish mythology fill the roles of nature  spirits guardians of the forest the  children are neither good nor evil the  others are also spirits of nature the  personification of winter it would  follow that if the children of the  forest are not evil then neither are the  others the nature of the other simply  does not jive with the nature of humans  coexistence does not seem possible that  being said it is important to note that  coexistence between humans and the  children also failed the children were  forced out of their own territory and  driven to almost complete extinction by  mankind this goes along with the theme  that appears throughout the story men  have difficulty living with nature and  instead seek to subdue and control it  that being said the inhabitants of the  world of Ice and Fire would not likely  consider the children to be demons in  their sense of the word there are many  other things that would be considered  demons in A Song of Ice and Fire however  many that even almost conformed to our  own modern view of the word let's take a  look at how demons are viewed within the  isang of Ice and Fire universe according  to Danny's blood riders a made he was a  woman who lay with demons and practiced  the blackest of sorcery in Abrahamic  mythology at the first woman Lilith was  said to have turned her back on God and  her husband Adam refusing to be  subservient she chose instead to lay  with demons and was cursed by God for it  this idea of women who lie with demons  is also common in many myths about  witches in the real world for power they  would become the brides of Satan himself  so the Dothraki view of a meiji a witch  as a woman who has lain with demons  aligns with many historical views on  witches in our own world as I mentioned  earlier demons are typically thought of  as sources or agents of evil  if gods were beings of benevolence than  demons would be the antithesis this  viewpoint does seem to be present in the  isang of ice and fire world the idea of  a demon is met with a negative  connotation demons in A Song of Ice and  Fire like in our own world are also  sometimes associated with Hell in a  Clash of Kings Arya wonders if roars and  biter were in fact not men and all and  in fact were demons that had been called  up from some Hell by Jack and Hagana  here you can see demons in the Song of  Ice and Fire universe are associated  with Hell so since so many of our real  world views on demons come from  Christianity we have to consider that  perhaps some of the views of the  Westerosi on demons arose from their own  analogue for Christianity which is of  course the faith of the seven this  religion which was brought to Westeros  by the Andals claims that there are both  seven heavens and seven hells descending  deeper and deeper  these hells were a place where sinners  would be punished the idea of layered  hell is reminiscent of the way the  Christian hell is portrayed in Dante's  Divine Comedy an epic poem that tells  the tale of a man journey through hell  and limbo and into heaven eventually  Dante's Inferno is the first cantika of  the Divine Comedy which totally changed  the way Christians viewed hell from that  point on  giving them a visceral view of what hell  may have been like Botticelli's painting  published 150 years later provided an  even more vivid picture depicting humans  being tortured by beings that could only  be described as demons like in our own  world throughout the world of A Song of  Ice and Fire demons are pretty much  always associated with malice corruption  and supernatural evil places that have  been deemed cursed are said to be demon  haunted there is also mention of human  dealings with demons which are always  looked negatively upon here are some  examples the smoking sea where Valyrian  met its doom was mentioned to be demon  hunted in a storm of sorts and a Clash  of Kings very says this to Tyrion when  his  arriving the circumstances of his  mutilation was it a god a demon some  conjurer's trick I could not tell you  and I know all the tricks all I can say  for certainty is that he called it and  it answered and since that day I have  hated magic and all those who practice  it  far north beyond the wall it was said  that Craster who we would later discover  gave his sons to the others quote  trafficked with slavers and demons the  magic of the others is actually referred  to multiple times as demonic in the  first book a game of rooms in a Jon Snow  chapter after the Lord Commander is  attacked by the undead corpse of a  former night's watchman it is stated  that whatever demonic force moved Oh  Thor had been driven out by the flames  and then there are the number of strange  entities set to be worshipped in many  queer places throughout their world  kejoro's Black Goat of the woods which  takes its name from Lovecraftian Bor the  pale child back Alon who was worshiped  in the Dark City of a shy and even rule  or the red God was considered to be a  demon by some like the gods of A Song of  Ice and Fire there are many demons  worshipped revered and feared and also  like the gods their existence can never  truly be verified only hinted at except  considering the children and the others  of course and then there are the  metaphorical demons  [Music]  take Arya Stark for example she was  present at her own father's unjust  execution ripped away from her family  and all that she had ever known forced  to take on other identities like re or  weasel in order to survive but who is  she on the inside  what is she becoming and what has she  become how do our is inner demons  manifest there's no doubt that they  exist and they grow as the books  continue and as traumatic things  continue to happen to Arya who let's not  forget is still a child  Arya makes her first kill in a game of  Thrones before Ned is executed  she had reacted out of terror using  needle to kill a stable boy who had  intended to take her to Queen Cersei  Arya does in fact fill guilt in this  moment it mentions that she fills the  need to get far away from the stables  away from the boys accusing eyes it is  also mentioned that at this point Arya  was still frightened in the face of  death  the next time Arya kills it is much more  deliberate and it does not have nearly  as much of an effect on her by that  point during her escape from Harrenhal  Arya has developed a coldness she kills  the guard in order to escape without any  remorse but remember this is after her  father's unjust execution after the  death of her friend Lommy and the  butcher's boy after being taken prisoner  and beaten Arya at this point is very  traumatized life in general has become  less valuable to her and this only  intensifies Arya's past trauma her  demons are contributing to the formation  of a very dark character Arya's past  trauma her demons manifest in deadly  ways throughout the series in the winds  of winter chapter mercy for instance we  see a version of Arya previously not  seen one that is willing to use  sexuality to lure and then coldly kill  someone who had wronged her in the past  I have said before that I find Aria Sark  in the books to be one of the most  disturbing with all that has happened to  her there's almost no way that she could  grow up without carrying tremendous  baggage with her and Aria is not the  only one  sandor clegane carries his trauma his  demons from his past within him it  manifests in his love of killing and his  fear of fire and perhaps there was  always some seed of cruelty within  Cersei but the witch's prophecy  certainly shaped the decisions that she  made this leads to her paranoid and  delusional behaviors arya was greatly  traumatized by several things but for  many all that takes is a single moment  to permit the entrance of a demon Ned  was tormented throughout book one by his  demons eaten alive by a secret that he  dared not utter allowed the young  graduate ORN his home as a boy and was  thrust into a world that he did not  recognize taken in by the Starks but  always knowing that he was not one of  them and never would be and the  rejection of his true family only  strengthened his demons no character in  this series is free from demons they  manifest in their own hatred of others  and of themselves they manifest in their  fears and doubts George RR Martin's  writing is brilliant because his  characters feel real in this way  none are perfect and all struggle with  some demon supernatural or otherwise  thank you guys so much for watching if  you enjoyed this video make sure you  like and subscribe  and if you want to support this channel  consider clicking the link in the  description to my patreon page
 

